                <pb facs="0573" n="491" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg491"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/1750.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Mexican
                    Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-05-25"><hi rendition="#italic">May 25,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 32.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Referring to your note of the 2d
                    instant, regarding the movement of arms and ammunition to Laredo and adjacent
                    points, especially to Fremont, where a merchant named J. C. Canales is reported
                    to be in collusion with Mexican insurgents, I have the honor to inform you that
                    the Department is advised by the Department of Justice, under date of the 10th
                    instant, that this information has been communicated to its officers in
                    Texas.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.],</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
